  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">SDC Support to the Sudan Response in Chad</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">On the morning of 15 April 2023, the Rapid Support Forces (RSF) launched an offensive against the Sudanese Armed Forces (SAF), leading to open conflict between the two parties in several Sudanese states. Since the outbreak of violence in Sudan, over 370,000 people have found refuge in Chad. 
 
Through this project, IOM aims to contribute to meeting the emergency needs of Chadian returnees from Sudan in the east of Chad through improving: 1) improving living conditions for vulnerable returnees in sites via shelter and settlements assistance, 2) improving access to clean water and hygiene for vulnerable returnees, and 3) supporting the social and economic reintegration of Chadian returnees displaced from Sudan.</narrative>
  </description>
